English version
================================================================================

"Software" means all files in this repository, including SKILL.md, guides/ and scripts/, and the
text, prompts, code and examples they contain. "You" means the individual or organization that
obtains the Software. "Licensor" means EmergenAI.

1. What you may do

1.1 Download, install and run the Software for any purpose, including commercial purposes. An
    organization may install the Software for its members to use within that organization.
1.2 Use the Software to make videos and other results ("Output"), and use the Output in any way,
    including commercially. The Output belongs to you; the Licensor claims no rights in it.
1.3 Modify the Software. A modified version may be used by you or within your organization; to
    publish it, section 1.4 applies.
1.4 Publish and redistribute the Software or a modified version of it free of charge, provided
    that:
    (a) you keep this license and the copyright notices, and credit the original author
        "EmergenAI" with a link to the official repository
        https://github.com/EmergenAI/video-recut in a prominent place;
    (b) for a modified version, you state prominently that "this version has been modified and is
        not the official version", and describe the main changes;
    (c) a modified version remains under this license and may not be released under any other
        license.
    A modified version published under this section does not breach sections 2.3 or 2.4.
1.5 Quote excerpts of the Software in articles, tutorials, reviews and similar content, provided
    that you credit the author "EmergenAI" with a link to the official repository. Quotations may
    not be used for any purpose prohibited by sections 2.3 or 2.4.

2. What you may not do

Unless you have the Licensor's prior written permission, you may not:

2.1 publish or redistribute the Software or any part of it (including a modified version)
    without crediting the author or without marking the modifications;
2.2 sell, rent, lend or sublicense the Software, or charge for it;
2.3 incorporate the Software or any part of it (including its text, prompts, workflows and code)
    into any other software, skill, plugin, online service or product, or offer the Software to
    others as a hosted service;
2.4 use the contents of the Software to build competing software, skills or services;
2.5 remove or alter the copyright notices in the Software or this license.

3. Permissions and contact

For any right listed in section 2, or for a commercial license, customization or partnership,
contact the Licensor through the official repository:
https://github.com/EmergenAI/video-recut

Persons designated by the Licensor in writing may modify and publish the Software within the scope
the Licensor authorizes.

4. Third-party software and services

Third-party software that the Software installs or invokes at run time is distributed under its
own license; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Content generated through the Bibei open platform or other
services is also subject to those services' terms.

5. Termination

If you breach this license, all rights granted to you under it end automatically, and you must
stop using and delete all copies of the Software. Output you lawfully made before termination is
not affected.

6. Disclaimer

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT
NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE, INCLUDING CHARGES
INCURRED ON THIRD-PARTY SERVICES WHILE USING THE SOFTWARE.
